f whey. Like other whey cheeses, it is made by coagulating the proteins that remain after the casein has been used to make cheese, notably albumin and globulin."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-ricotta"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ricotta"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":5,"groups":[["Italian cuisine","cuisine/italian-cuisine",[["Cassatella di sant'Agata","dish/cassatella-di-sant-agata"],["Crostata","dish/crostata"]]],["Sicilian cuisine","cuisine/sicilian-cuisine",[["Iris (pastry)","dish/iris-pastry"],["Pasta alla Norma","dish/pasta-alla-norma"]]],["Italian-American cuisine","cuisine/italian-american-cuisine",[["Rollatini","dish/rollatini"]]],["Maltese cuisine","cuisine/maltese-cuisine",[["Pastizz","dish/pastizz"]]],["Neapolitan cuisine","cuisine/neapolitan-cuisine",[["Pastiera","dish/pastiera"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Eggplant","ingredient/eggplant"],["Candied peel","ingredient/candied-peel"],["Ceramic glaze","ingredient/ceramic-glaze"],["Fruit juice","ingredient/fruit-juice"],["Icing","ingredient/icing"],["Liqueur","ingredient/liqueur"],["Marzipan","ingredient/marzipan"],["Sponge cake","ingredient/sponge-cake"],["Succade","ingredient/succade"],["Sugar","ingredient/sugar"],["Custard","ingredient/custard"],["Jam","ingredient/jam"],["Nutella","ingredient/nutella"],["Shortcrust pastry","ingredient/shortcrust-pastry"],["Basil","ingredient/basil"],["Garlic","ingredient/garlic"]]}],"img":{"src":"/world-cuisine/img/thumb/f/ff/Ricotte_fresche.jpg/500px-Ricotte_fresche.jpg","w":500,"h":333,"by":"8w9d","lic":"CC0","licUrl":"http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/deed.en","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ricotte_fresche.jpg"}},"dish/coniglio-alla-sanremese":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/coniglio-alla-sanremese","n":"Coniglio alla sanremese","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Ligurian cuisine","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["Coniglio alla sanremese is an Italian recipe based on rabbit, cooked and served with a sauce enriched with olives, walnuts and herbs. It is a traditional dish of Ligurian cuisine, originating in the town of Sanremo; variations of the recipe, under the name coniglio alla ligure, are spread all over Liguria."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-coniglio-alla-sanremese"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coniglio_alla_sanremese"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Ligurian cuisine","cuisine/cuisine-of-liguria"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":1,"links":[["Rabbit meat","ingredient/rabbit-meat"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"A Small Kitchen in Genoa","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"asmallkitcheningenoa.com","note":"Genoese cook Enrica Monzani's English-language blog of Ligurian recipes.","url":"https://asmallkitcheningenoa.com/about","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Ligurian cuisine","links":[["Baxin","dish/baxin"]]}],"img":{"src":"/world-cuisine/img/thumb/7/73/Coniglio_olive_pinoli.jpg/500px-Coniglio_olive_pinoli.jpg","w":500,"h":330,"by":"F Ceragioli","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coniglio_olive_pinoli.jpg"}},"dish/giardiniera":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/giardiniera","n":"Giardiniera","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Italian cuisine","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["Giardiniera is an Italian relish of pickled vegetables in vinegar or oil."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-giardiniera"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Giardiniera"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Italian cuisine","cuisine/italian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Pasta Grannies","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"pastagrannies.substack.com","note":"Vicky Bennison's long-running video series filming Italian grandmothers making regional pasta by hand.","url":"